-- title:
--   Corestriction descent of corner submodules and corner Hecke rings
-- statement:
--   Let $L\ge 1$, let $S\subseteq\mathbb N$, and let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal ideal, with residue field $k$. Let $H,H'\le(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ with [`CohCarrier.LevelLE L L H' H 1`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330), i.e. every $u\in H$ has its image in $H'$, and suppose some $r\mid L$ with $r\ge 4$ satisfies $u\equiv 1 \bmod r$ for all $u\in H'$. Let $\varphi\colon G\to$ [`CohCarrier.Gen L S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) pick, for each index, one of $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$), $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid L$) or $\langle d\rangle$, and assume the family contains $\langle u\rangle$ for every $u\in H'$ (via $dG$) and that the resulting operators on $H^1=\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L)^{\mathrm{ab}},\mathcal O)$, respectively on $\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_{H'}(L)^{\mathrm{ab}},\mathcal O)$, commute pairwise. Let $\bar\theta\colon G\to k$, let $\mathbb T_H,\mathbb T_{H'}$ be the $\mathcal O$-subalgebras of endomorphisms generated by these operators, let `Sp`, `Sp'` be complete orthogonal idempotent splittings of $\mathbb T_H$, $\mathbb T_{H'}$ indexed by their maximal ideals, let $i_0,i_0'$ be indices, and let $\pi,\pi'$ be $\mathcal O$-algebra maps from the corner rings $e_{i_0}\mathbb T_He_{i_0}$, $e_{i_0'}\mathbb T_{H'}e_{i_0'}$ to $k$ sending the image of each generator to $\bar\theta(g)$. Then, for the corestriction map $j=$ [`CohCarrier.jDegL L L H' H 1 𝒪 𝒪 h`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L492) from level $H$ to level $H'$: (i) $j$ carries $e_{i_0}H^1(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal O)$ onto $e_{i_0'}H^1(\Gamma_{H'}(L),\mathcal O)$ as $\mathcal O$-submodules; (ii) for $m$ in $e_{i_0}H^1$, $j(m)=0$ if and only if $m$ lies in the $\mathcal O$-span of the elements $\langle u\rangle x-x$ with $u\in H'$ and $x\in e_{i_0}H^1$; and (iii) there is a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\Phi$ from $e_{i_0}\mathbb T_He_{i_0}$ to $e_{i_0'}\mathbb T_{H'}e_{i_0'}$ sending the corner image of each generator at level $H$ to that of the same generator at level $H'$ and satisfying $j(z\cdot m)=\Phi(z)\cdot j(m)$ for all $z$ in the corner ring and all $m\in e_{i_0}H^1$.
--
--   This is the descent step of the Taylor–Wiles argument in cohomological form: corestriction from $\Gamma_H(L)$ to $\Gamma_{H'}(L)$ identifies the localised weight-two cohomology at the higher level with the coinvariants of the diamond action of $H'$, and transports the local Hecke ring of an arbitrary commuting subfamily of operators. It is used in the computation of a basis and of the rank of the corner submodule over the relevant group ring when the residual system of eigenvalues is not Eisenstein.
